# A kernel stack overflow runs into the unmapped guard page below the stack.
# The page fault cannot be pushed onto the dead stack, so the CPU raises a
# double fault, which runs on IST1 and reports, instead of silently
# corrupting memory (docs/design.md, "Kernel entry and exit", Invariants).
cmdline: test=stack_overflow
exit: failure
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: recursing until the kernel stack overflows
expect: KERNEL PANIC at kernel/src/arch/x86_64/trap.rs:
expect: DF double fault (vector 8) in ring 0
expect: frame on IST1
